  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "util-linux security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for util-linux is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "The util-linux package contains a random collection of files that implements some low-level basic linux utilities.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nutil-linux is a random collection of Linux utilities. Before util-linux 2.41.4, `parse_dos_extended()` in `libblkid/src/partitions/dos.c` computes an extended-partition start sector with 32-bit addition and does not apply the extended-area bounds checks to the first two EBR entries. A local attacker who causes a crafted DOS extended-partition disk image or removable medium to be probed can wrap `cur_start + start` to sector zero and cause libblkid to report a false partition overlapping the MBR. This directly compromises the integrity of the reported partition metadata; disk modification or availability loss requires a separate downstream consumer to act on that metadata. This issue is fixed in 2.41.4.(CVE-2026-53615)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for util-linux is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "util-linux",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
